> Fig. 2 | Analytical framework for estimating the ocean-based social cost of
> carbon. This diagram presents the structured analytical framework developed
> to quantify the blue SCC by integrating biophysical and economic valuation
> functions. The process starts with a literature search—screening studies that
> quantify climate-induced impacts on ocean-based assets or marine ecosystems.
> An in-depth analysis follows, focusing on the four types of blue capital identified:
> corals, mangroves, fisheries and mariculture, and seaports. Within each capital
> block, the diagram briefly presents the underlying biophysical and economic
> valuation studies that were selected. Each block highlights the types of value
> accounted for: market values, non-market use values and non-use values, as
