> Model parameterization
> The value estimates that go into the utility function come from different
> approaches. For corals and mangroves, we first simulate the change in
> country-level cover area Ab c, t and then multiply it by their shadow price
> pb, v
> c, t , with b = {corals, mangroves} and v = {non-use, non-market use}.
> Coral area cover changes as a linear function of temperature, based on
> ref. 27, and the mangrove cover changes as a quadratic function of
> temperature, based on ref. 28. The shadow price is obtained from the
> updated ecosystem services valuation database (ESVD) as presented
> in ref. 53. Following ref. 15, the value of corals market use and non-use
> values increases over time with the rate of growth of GDP per capita, as
> pcorals, v
